--- p=19,23: H from canon, c3/c5 exact (full a1 infeasible) ---
  H(Interval) > H(Paley) at p=19,23 (canon THM-135/137).
  Since Paley maximizes EVERY c_ell (level 1), alpha_1(P)>alpha_1(I),
  so the level-1 term 2*alpha_1 still FAVORS Paley at p=19,23.
  Yet H(I)>H(P) => the levels j>=2 term R MUST favor Interval by MORE.
  => the crossover is carried ENTIRELY by the packing levels j>=2.
  p=19: H(I)-H(P) = +11517077848
  p=23: H(I)-H(P) = +251330514177930
